license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For every n >= 8, every Berge-triangle-free triple system on n vertices with more than floor((n-1)^2/8) edges is a spanning subsystem of a paired product F(n,p). Hence the Berge-triangle saturation spectrum above this threshold consists exactly of the sizes p(n-2p), and the threshold is sharp because a saturated system that is not a paired product exists at it. The window contains n/4 - O(sqrt n) missing sizes, given by explicit quadratic deficits. Exact checkers and a Lean proof that paired products are saturated are included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
